f98cdb2fc47f9a1c613c673bfc2255adc31546df:docs/research/ramsey-number-5-5/index.html:115:        <p>This is a genuine complete exclusion of one finite endpoint, not a statistical observation. It rests on an elementary capacity inequality, a byte-pinned exhaustive calculation over 62,382 catalog pairs, and a short equality-rigidity argument. Its catalog completeness and nonisomorphism assumptions remain external published inputs.</p>
